        "title": "CLI 1.0.682 adds Freebuff first-time onboarding suggested prompts",
        "summary": "CLI release 1.0.682 ships clickable starter prompts for first-time Freebuff users, rendered above the input bar on a pristine, idle, empty default-mode chat via SuggestedPrompts imported from cli/src/components/suggested-prompts. chat.tsx initializes showSuggestedPrompts from IS_FREEBUFF && !hasSubmittedFirstPrompt() and retires it through markFirstPromptSubmitted() once the first prompt is sent, persisting the hasSubmittedFirstPrompt flag added to Settings in cli/src/utils/settings.ts. The component defines DEFAULT_SUGGESTED_PROMPTS plus LABEL_DESCRIPTION_GAP = 2 and MIN_WIDTH_FOR_DESCRIPTION = 80, though the diff does not show terminalWidth being compared against MIN_WIDTH_FOR_DESCRIPTION within this commit, and emits SUGGESTED_PROMPT_SHOWN and SUGGESTED_PROMPT_CLICKED analytics events newly added to common/src/constants/analytics-events.ts.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "cli/src/chat.tsx imports SuggestedPrompts, DEFAULT_SUGGESTED_PROMPTS, and SuggestedPromptSelection from cli/src/components/suggested-prompts; initializes showSuggestedPrompts via useState(() => IS_FREEBUFF && !hasSubmittedFirstPrompt()); retires prompts with markFirstPromptSubmitted() when messages.length > 0; and tracks SUGGESTED_PROMPT_SHOWN and SUGGESTED_PROMPT_CLICKED via common/src/constants/analytics-events.ts. cli/src/components/suggested-prompts.tsx is a new file exporting DEFAULT_SUGGESTED_PROMPTS and SuggestedPromptSelection, with LABEL_DESCRIPTION_GAP = 2 defined but not referenced elsewhere, and MIN_WIDTH_FOR_DESCRIPTION = 80 defined but never imported or checked against terminalWidth in this commit. cli/src/utils/settings.ts adds hasSubmittedFirstPrompt?: boolean to Settings with loadSettings and saveSettings validation, plus hasSubmittedFirstPrompt() and markFirstPromptSubmitted(). cli/release/package.json bumps version from 1.0.681 to 1.0.682.",
        "userVisible": true,
