      "facts": [
        "SIGKILL is the only signal that's portable across Linux/macOS/Windows here; SIGTERM may be ignored by the renderer on some platforms.",
        "Negative gate first: a known fatal marker gives us a more specific error message than \"no boot signal found\" would.",
        "Positive gate: the binary must have rendered a known boot screen.",
        "Negative gate first: a known fatal marker gives us a more specific error message than \"no boot signal found\" would. Both gates would fire on a crash; preferring the negative one just makes the failure log clearer.",
        "Deterministic crash, a known fatal marker is a real regression, not a flaky hang, so fail immediately without burning the remaining retries."
      ],
