        "v": 5,
        "title": "smoke-binary retries boot 3 times",
        "summary": "cli/scripts/smoke-binary.ts adds MAX_BOOT_ATTEMPTS = 3 to retry boot detection on transient Windows runner hangs. runBootAttempt isolates spawn and output capture, returning an AttemptOutcome union. Negative gate first: known fatal markers fail immediately without retrying. Positive gate: boot signal match exits 0; no-signal triggers next attempt.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:14:21.827Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The test that checks if the program starts up properly now tries three times instead of giving up after one failure. This helps because sometimes the test server has a temporary hiccup where the program doesn't start fast enough, and retrying usually fixes it. If the test detects a real problem (like a crash), it still fails right away without retrying, so actual bugs are caught just as quickly. The change only affects the automated tests that run on the build system, not your experience using the program.",
